WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.964
This work introduces Inverse Transition Learning,

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:05.821
a gradient free and constraint based approach.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:11.660
It converts a near optimal expert policy into a set
of constraints on the transition dynamics,

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:17.126
and then clips a Bayesian posterior over the
dynamics so that every sampled model yields

00:00:17.206 --> 00:00:19.238
a safe and high performing policy.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:20.791
Beyond the method itself,

00:00:20.871 --> 00:00:26.195
the paper carefully analyzes when and why maximum
likelihood estimation of the dynamics

00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:28.617
breaks down under uneven data coverage,

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:34.270
and it shows how combining the constraints with
uncertainty produces an informative ranking

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.500
of actions in the states where the expert is unsure.
